There are no automated tests.

Useful test dimensions would include:
- head-on equal-mass collision;
- glancing collision;
- overlap separation;
- wall bounce at each boundary;
- no double-processing of pair if algorithm is optimized;
- cursor-away vector direction;
- object initialization within viewport;
- deterministic seeded positions for regression;
- performance benchmark at N=50/150/500.

Browser visual output provides manual feedback, but it is not enough to validate the physics equations or performance envelope.

